    {
      "id": "PR6-ASSERTION-P1",
      "severity": "P1",
      "path": "media_kit_video/test/hdr_decoder_review_test.dart",
      "detail": "Incoming changes replace the existing observed-decoder-between-rounds failure test with a logical-name success test. Retaining Session source alone does not retain this gather assertion. Keep the entire public old rejection test and all public A/B, timeout, epoch, superseded, malformed/native-DV tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "PR6-FIXTURE-P2",
      "severity": "P2",
      "path": "media_kit_video/test/hdr_decoder_review_test.dart",
      "detail": "AVC/copy success fixture is internally much better, but its comment claims absent hwdec/gamma/primaries while it actually prepopulates all three and only clears pixel. MIME-negative is already complete on first round, so its betweenRounds callback is not invoked. Do not call these a verified complete real-device replay or evidence of cross-round protection."
    },
